# Analytics View Documentation: `screening_participation_rate`

## 1. Overview & Purpose

The `screening_participation_rate` view calculates organisation-level participation metrics for health screening programmes. It measures the percentage of eligible programme participants who successfully completed an approved screening, incorporating station-level deduplication, multi-table schema fallbacks, and zero-denominator safety logic.

---

## 2. SQL View Definition

```sql
CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW screening_participation_rate AS

WITH eligible_participations AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT
        p.participation_id,
        COALESCE(e.organisation_id, pr.organisation_id) AS organisation_id
    FROM participations p
    LEFT JOIN employees e
        ON e.employee_id = p.employee_id
    LEFT JOIN programmes pr
        ON pr.programme_id = p.programme_id
    WHERE 
        LOWER(TRIM(p.attendance_status)) = 'attended'
        AND COALESCE(e.organisation_id, pr.organisation_id) IS NOT NULL
),

approved_screenings AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT
        s.participation_id
    FROM screenings s
    INNER JOIN eligible_participations ep
        ON ep.participation_id = s.participation_id
    WHERE
        LOWER(TRIM(s.status)) IN ('completed', 'approved')
)

SELECT
    ep.organisation_id,
    
    -- Denominator: Total distinct eligible participants
    COUNT(DISTINCT ep.participation_id) AS eligible_participant_count,
    
    -- Numerator: Total distinct eligible participants with an approved/completed screening
    COUNT(DISTINCT aps.participation_id) AS screened_participant_count,
    
    -- Participation Rate Percentage
    ROUND(
        (
            COUNT(DISTINCT aps.participation_id)::NUMERIC 
            / NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT ep.participation_id), 0)
        ) * 100.0,
        2
    ) AS screening_participation_rate_pct

FROM eligible_participations ep
LEFT JOIN approved_screenings aps
    ON aps.participation_id = ep.participation_id
GROUP BY
    ep.organisation_id;
```

---

## 3. Key Calculations & Formulas

### Core Calculation

$$
\text{Participation Rate (\%)} = \left( \frac{\text{Screened Eligible Participants}}{\text{Total Eligible Participants}} \right) \times 100
$$

### Mathematical Definitions

1. **Total Eligible Participants (Denominator):**
   $$
   \text{Denominator} = \vert{} \{ p \in \text{Participations} \mid \text{attendance\_status}(p) = \text{'attended'} \land \text{org}(p) = o \} \vert{}
   $$

2. **Screened Participants (Numerator):**
   $$
   \text{Numerator} = \vert{} \{ p \in \text{Participations}_{\text{eligible}} \mid \exists s \in \text{Screenings}(s.\text{participation\_id} = p.\text{participation\_id} \land \text{status}(s) \in \{\text{'completed'}, \text{'approved'}\}) \} \vert{}
   $$

